           ever pushed to out_instrs), unlike the same-shaped plain
           `Instr::Assign` (tag 18) just above, which already has this
           obj_tok/fld_tok case. Found immediately after fixing
           parse_assign_target_op_pos's DOT/COLONCOLON tag mixup
           (parser.sv0) let a bare field-assignment statement parse at
           all: `q.x = 5;` then round-tripped correctly, but `q.x += 3;`
           still silently vanished — traced here, one layer downstream.
